.TH SHEDMAN-STATUS 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman-status \- aggregated dashboard across the four waybar signals
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman status
.br
.B shedman status
.RB { -j | --json }
.br
.B shedman status
.RB { -w | --watch }
.RB [ --interval
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman status
runs all four waybar-backed signal binaries
.RB ( shedman " " updates ", "
.BR shedman " " conflicts ", "
.BR shedman " " health ", "
.BR shedman " " doctor )
in
.B --waybar
mode and prints a single-screen summary plus a verdict line. Each
signal is run with a 2-second timeout; failures degrade gracefully
to
.IB unavailable ( error )
on that row only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
default (no flag)
Render a one-line-per-signal text dashboard plus a Summary line
(OK / Attention needed / N unavailable).
.TP
.BR -j , " --json"
Emit an aggregated JSON document
.RI ( schema:1 )
that passes each underlying
.B --waybar
payload through verbatim under its signal key, plus a top-level
summary section. Suitable for monitoring scripts.
.TP
.BR -w , " --watch"
Spawn a Textual TUI that re-runs the four probes on a timer and
re-renders. Press
.B q
to quit.
.TP
.BI --interval " N"
Refresh interval in seconds for
.BR --watch .
Default 5; minimum 1. Also overridable via
.BR SHEDOS_STATUS_INTERVAL .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHEDOS_STATUS_LIBEXEC
Override
.IR /usr/libexec/shedman .
Used by tests; rarely set by end users.
.TP
.B SHEDOS_STATUS_INTERVAL
Default refresh interval for
.BR --watch .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Always (the verdict is in the output, not the exit code).
.TP
.B 2
.I /usr/libexec/shedman
isn't a directory \(em the env override is wrong, or shedos-system
is broken.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman (1).
